<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Draper</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1721–1787</span> · Also known as Sir William Draper</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir William Draper was a British army officer who led the expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in October 1762 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. He later served as lieutenant governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Minorca</a> and is remembered for his public exchange with the anonymous writer Junius.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-draper.jpg" alt="William Draper" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Gainsborough · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_William_Draper_KB.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
